INSERT INTO `holidays` VALUES (1,'Ram Nawami/World Theatre Day','Rama Navami is a Hindu festival that celebrates the birth of Rama, a revered deity in Hinduism, also known as the seventh avatar of Lord Vishnu.','2026-03-27','2026-03-22 10:29:13'),(2,'Nepali New Year 2083','Baisakh 1 marks the first day of the new year in the Bikram Sambat (B.S.) calendar, which is the official calendar used in Nepal. It is known locally as Nava Varsha or Naya Barsha.','2026-04-14','2026-03-22 10:34:49'),(11,'Buddha Jayanti/International Labor Day','Buddha Jayanti, also known as Buddha Purnima or Vesak, is a major festival celebrating the birth, enlightenment, and death (Parinirvana) of Siddhartha Gautama (Lord Buddha). Celebrated on the full moon in April/May, it features prayers, meditation, and charity. Majdoor Diwas is known in English as Labour Day or International Workers\' Day, and is also popularly referred to as May Day. Celebrated on May 1st every year, this public holiday honors the achievements, contributions, and rights of the working class, often featuring rallies and solidarity marches for workers\' rights','2026-05-01','2026-03-22 10:41:06'),(17,'Ganatantra Diwas/Republic Day','Ganatantra Diwas, or Republic Day, in Nepal is observed annually on Jestha 15 according to the Nepali calendar.  according to the Nepali calendar, which generally corresponds to May 28 or 29. It commemorates the historic day in 2008 when the Constituent Assembly formally declared Nepal a Federal Democratic Republic.','2026-05-29','2026-03-22 10:45:37'),(32,'Janai Purnima','Janai Purnima is a Hindu festival celebrated all over the country, with family get togethers and feasts of Kwati or sprout lentils. This day is also a harbinger of rejuvenation with Hindu men renewing their ‪Janai and people flocking to Shiva temples in different parts of the country.','2026-08-28','2026-03-22 10:56:33'),(33,'Gai Jatra/Weekly Holiday','Gai Jatra, or the \"Cow Festival,\" is a significant annual Hindu festival in Nepal (typically Aug-Sept) that commemorates deceased loved ones with a blend of grief and celebratory satire. Originating in the Malla era to comfort a mourning queen, families parade cows or children dressed as cows, transforming personal loss into a shared community celebration of life.','2026-08-29','2026-03-22 10:57:13'),(34,'Shree Krishna Janmasahtami','Krishna Janmashtami also known simply as Krishnashtami, Janmashtami, or Gokulashtami, is an annual Hindu festival that celebrates the birth of Krishna, the eighth avatar of Vishnu. ','2026-09-04','2026-03-22 10:58:42'),(37,'Haritalika Teej','Hartalika Teej - Women\'s Festival of Nepal 14th September ...Hartalika Teej is a sacred Hindu festival celebrated primarily by women in Nepal and northern India to honor the devotion of Goddess Parvati to Lord Shiva. Women fast strictly (often nirjala, without water) for marital bliss, long life for husbands, or a good partner, typically wearing red/green attire, dancing, and praying.','2026-09-14','2026-03-22 11:00:10'),(38,'Constitution Day/Weekly Holiday','Sambidhan Diwas (Constitution Day) is celebrated in Nepal annually on Asoj 3rd (around September 19-20) to commemorate the promulgation of the Constitution of Nepal in 2072 B.S. (2015 A.D.). It marks the transition to a federal democratic republic, upholding principles of inclusivity, secularism, and social justice, with nationwide celebrations including flag-hoisting and lighting lamps.','2026-09-19','2026-03-22 11:01:33'),(39,'Indra Jatra','Indra Jatra, locally known as Yenya, is a vibrant eight-day religious festival in Kathmandu, Nepal, usually held in September to honor Indra, the king of heaven and god of rain. It features the raising of a ceremonial pole (Yosin), dramatic masked dances (Lakhay), and a, chariot procession of the Living Goddess Kumari.','2026-09-25','2026-03-22 11:02:03'),(40,'Jitiya Parva','Jitiya (or Jivitputrika) is a rigorous three-day Hindu fasting festival observed by mothers in Nepal and parts of India (Bihar, UP, Jharkhand) for the longevity, health, and prosperity of their children. Celebrated in Ashwin Krishna Paksha (Sep/Oct), mothers observe a strictly nirjala (waterless) fast on Ashtami, following the \"Naha-Khai\" ritual.','2026-10-04','2026-03-22 11:05:16'),(41,'Ghatasthapana','Ghatasthapana, or Kalash Sthapana, is the sacred, ritualistic commencement of the nine-day Navratri festival, marking the installation of a holy pot (\r\n) symbolizing Goddess Durga. Occurring on the first day of Ashwin (September-October), it involves planting barley seeds in soil, nurturing them until Dashami for growth and prosperity. ','2026-10-11','2026-03-22 11:08:27'),(43,'Dashain Holiday','','2026-10-19','2026-03-22 11:09:47'),(44,'Maha Astami','','2026-10-18','2026-03-22 11:10:05'),(45,'Maha Nawami','Dashain Holiday','2026-10-20','2026-03-22 11:10:23'),(46,'Bijayaa Dashami','Dashain Holiday','2026-10-21','2026-03-22 11:10:34'),(47,'Dashain Holiday','Dashain Holiday','2026-10-22','2026-03-22 11:11:05'),(48,'Kaag Tihar','Kaag Tihar is the first day of the five-day Tihar festival in Nepal (and Wikipedia among Hindus), celebrated on Kartik Krishna Triodashi. It honors crows as messengers of Yamaraj (the God of Death), with people offering food and worship to ensure peace and ward off bad omens.','2026-11-07','2026-03-22 11:11:58'),(49,'Laxmi Puja','Lakshmi Puja, Sanskrit: लक्ष्मीपूजा, romanized: Lakṣmīpūjā, Bengali/Assamese: লক্ষ্মী পূজা is a Hindu occasion for the veneration of Lakshmi, the goddess of prosperity and the Supreme Goddess of Vaishnavism.','2026-11-08','2026-03-22 11:12:49'),(50,'Gai Tihar','Gai Puja (Cow Worship) is a significant Hindu festival observed, primarily in Nepal, on the third day of the Tihar festival (Kartik Krishna Aunsi). Cows are revered as Goddess Lakshmi (prosperity) and mothers, adorned with garlands, fed delicacies, and worshipped to express gratitude for their nourishment','2026-11-09','2026-03-22 11:13:27'),(52,'Govardhan Puja','Govardhan Puja or Annakut, is a Hindu festival celebrated on the first lunar day of the bright fortnight of the month of Kartika, on the fourth day of Diwali. Devotees worship an image of Govardhan Hill made out of cow dung and prepare and offer a large variety of vegetarian food to Krishna as a mark of gratitude.','2026-11-10','2026-03-22 11:14:03'),(53,'Bhai Tika/Kija Puja','Bhai Tika (or Bhai Dooj) is a5th-day festival of Tihar in Nepal (similar to Bhai Dooj in India), celebrating the deep bond between brothers and sisters. Sisters apply a special seven-coloured tika (Saptarangi) and garlands on their brothers, praying for long life, while brothers offer gifts and protection.','2026-11-11','2026-03-22 11:14:52'),(54,'Chhath Parva','Chhath is an ancient Indo-Nepalese Hindu festival, native to eastern India and southern Nepal. It is celebrated especially in the Indian states of Bihar, Jharkhand, West Bengal and Uttar Pradesh; and Koshi, Gandaki, Bagmati, Lumbini, and Madhesh provinces of Nepal.','2026-11-15','2026-03-22 11:15:27'),(55,'Guru Nanak Jayanti','Guru Nanak Gurpurab, also known as Guru Nanak Prakash Utsav and Guru Nanak Jayanti, celebrates the birth of the first Sikh guru, Guru Nanak. One of the most celebrated and important Sikh gurus and the founder of Sikhism, Guru Nanak is highly revered by the Sikh community.','2026-11-24','2026-03-22 11:17:34'),(56,'Ubhauli Parva','Ubhauli Parva is a vibrant, annual festival celebrated by the Kirat community (Rai, Limbu, Yakkha, Sunuwar) in Nepal, usually falling on Baisakh Purnima (April–May). It marks the beginning of the planting season and signifies the upward migration of people and birds to higher, cooler altitudes to escape the summer heat.','2026-12-04','2026-03-22 11:18:38'),(57,'Christmas Day','hristmas Day, celebrated annually on December 25th, is a major Christian festival commemorating the birth of Jesus Christ, marking a significant religious and cultural holiday worldwide. Traditions include gift-giving, decorating trees, church services, and feasts, with roots in both Christian theology and older winter festivals.','2026-12-25','2026-03-22 11:20:03'),(58,'Tamhu Lohsar','Tamu Losar is the New Year festival of the Gurung community (Tamu) in Nepal, celebrated annually on Poush 15th (late December/early January) to mark the start of the Tamu Sambat calendar. It signifies the end of winter and a prosperous new harvest, celebrated with traditional, cultural, and social activities.','2026-12-30','2026-03-22 11:20:42'),(59,'Prithivi Jayanti','Prithvi Jayanti is a holiday annually celebrated on 11 January to commemorate the birth of King Prithvi Narayan Shah, who was the first king of unified Nepal. In the mid-18th century, he set out to unify the small kingdoms which would become present-day Nepal.','2027-01-11','2026-03-22 11:21:42'),(60,'Maghe Sankranti','Maghe Sakranti marks the beginning of the Nepali month of Magh and is celebrated as Maghe Sankranti, the first day of the sun\'s northern journey (Uttarayan). It signals the end of the winter solstice, with celebrations including eating traditional food like ghee, chaaku, and tarul, and serves as the New Year for the Tharu community.','2027-01-15','2026-03-22 11:22:38'),(61,'Martyr\'s Day','Shahid Diwas (Martyrs\' Day) is observed in Nepal annually on Magh 16 (typically late January) to honor those who sacrificed their lives for democracy, freedom, and sovereignty.','2027-01-30','2026-03-22 11:24:24'),(62,'Sonam Lohsar','Sonam Lhochhar is a New Year\'s day festival of the Tamang and Hyolmo people of Nepal as well as Sikkim and Darjeeling regions of India. It falls on the second new moon after the winter solstice which is usually the Magh Sukla Pratipada based on the eastern lunar calendar.','2027-02-07','2026-03-22 11:25:27'),(63,'Democracy Day/Prajatantra Diwas','Prajatantra Divas, or National Democracy Day, is celebrated annually in Nepal on Falgun 7 (typically February 19) to commemorate the end of the 104-year-long Rana autocracy in 1951. It marks the establishment of democracy and the victory of the people\'s movement. The day is honored with public, government, and cultural celebrations. ','2027-02-19','2026-03-22 11:26:25'),(64,'Maha Shivaratri','Maha Shivaratri is a Hindu festival celebrated annually to worship the deity Shiva, between February and March.[4] According to the Hindu calendar, The festival is observed on the chaturdashi (14th lunar day) of krishna paksha (waning moon) of the month of Magha or Phalguna','2027-03-06','2026-03-22 11:27:37'),(65,'International Women\'s Day','International Women\'s Day is celebrated on 8 March, commemorating women\'s fight for equality and liberation along with the women\'s rights movement. International Women\'s Day gives focus to issues such as gender equality, reproductive rights, and violence and abuse against women.','2027-03-08','2026-03-22 11:28:13'),(66,'Gyalpo Losar','Gyalpo Losar s the new year festival of the Sherpa people celebrated in Nepal and the Indian state of Sikkim along with the neighbouring Darjeeling and Kalimpong districts.','2027-03-08','2026-03-22 11:28:54'),(67,'Fagu Poornima/Holi','Fagu Purnima, commonly known as Holi, is a vibrant Hindu festival of colors celebrated in Nepal and India, marking the end of winter and the arrival of spring. It symbolizes the triumph of good over evil (Holika Dahan) and is celebrated on the full moon day in Falgun (Feb/March) by smearing colors, dancing, and sharing sweets.','2027-03-21','2026-03-22 11:30:19'),(68,'Fagu Poornima/Terai Holi','Fagu Purnima, commonly known as Holi, is a vibrant Hindu festival of colors celebrated in Nepal and India, marking the end of winter and the arrival of spring. It symbolizes the triumph of good over evil (Holika Dahan) and is celebrated on the full moon day in Falgun (Feb/March) by smearing colors, dancing, and sharing sweets.','2027-03-22','2026-03-22 11:30:28'),(69,'Ghode Jatra','Ghode Jatra is a horse festival native to Kathmandu. The festival occurs annually in mid-March or early April. In the festival, a horse parades is organized in Tundikhel. The parade and competitions is carried out in the presence of heads of state. Nepal Army organizes the parade and competitions.','2027-04-06','2026-03-22 11:31:16'),(70,'Official Trip','Closing, Refreshment','2026-07-17','2026-07-20 16:00:50');
/*!40000 ALTER TABLE `holidays` ENABLE KEYS */;
